For \(P(x) = ax + b\) to have 4 as a root, \(P(4) = 0\), and so \(4a + b = 0\).

Now we need to find all the pairs \((a, b)\) that satisfy the equation \(4a + b = 0\) with \(a, b \in \{-7, -6, \ldots, -1, 0, 1, \ldots, 6, 7\}\).

With the restriction that not only do we need to have 4 as a root, but also the polynomial must be non-zero (i.e., \(a \neq 0\)), we need to consider all values for \(a\) except 0, and find the corresponding \(b\).
