To find the probability, we need the area of the region where \(|y| < 2 - |x|\) within the bounds of \(S\), and then divide by the total area of \(S\).

The total area of \(S\) is the area of the two triangles, each with base and height of 2, so the total area is \(2 \times \frac{1}{2} \times 2 \times 2 = 4\).

