(1) We find the first derivative of \( f(x) \), and determine where it is positive (indicating monotonic increase).
(2) If the function is monotonically increasing on all of \( \mathbb{R} \), then the derivative must be non-negative everywhere.
(3) We need to find values of \( a \) for which the derivative changes sign at \( x = 0 \), indicating a possible inflection point.
</think>

