- \(\overrightarrow{AD} = D - A = \left( 0 - 1, 0 - 1, 1 - 1 \right) = (-1, -1, 0)\)

The cosine of the angle \(\theta\) between these vectors is given by the dot product formula:
\[
\cos \theta = \frac{\overrightarrow{MN} \cdot \overrightarrow{AD}}{\|\overrightarrow{MN}\| \|\overrightarrow{AD}\|}
\]
</think>

<python>
import numpy as np

# Vectors MN and AD
MN = np.array([-1, 0, 0])
AD = np.array([-1, -1, 0])

# Dot product
dot_product = np.dot(MN, AD)

# Magnitudes of the vectors
magnitude_MN = np.linalg.norm(MN)
magnitude_AD = np.linalg.norm(AD)

# Cosine of the angle
cos_theta = dot_product / (magnitude_MN * magnitude_AD)
theta = np.arccos(cos_theta)

# Convert to degrees
theta_degrees = np.degrees(theta)
print(theta_degrees)
