To solve this problem, we need to express the area and perimeter of the rectangle in terms of its side lengths, which we will call a and b. We then need to find which of the given numbers cannot be equal to the sum of a, b, 2a, and 2b. Simplifying this gives us the equation A + P = 2a + 2b + ab. We will iterate through the possible side lengths a and b looking for A + P values and check which of the given options cannot be achieved.
