<result> To find the greatest possible total number of balls in two boxes, we need to ensure that when picking 3 balls from the first box, there is guaranteed to be at least one blue ball, when picking 4 balls from the second box, there is guaranteed to be at least one red ball, and when picking 5 balls from either box or both, there is guaranteed to be at least one white ball. This is a constraint on the composition of the balls in the boxes.
